          "reason": "The stated map T_n has p>=1 and n>=1 and uses mean n^{-1}sum_i x_i on exactly n records. Proof1.1 gives a polynomial map from that nonempty data space; an empty sample n=0 is excluded rather than interpreted through the undefined1/n coefficient.",
          "reviewed": {
            "upheld": true,
            "by": "owner-delegated-focused-boundary-review",
            "reason": "The stated map T_n has p>=1 and n>=1 and uses mean n^{-1}sum_i x_i on exactly n records. Proof1.1 gives a polynomial map from that nonempty data space; an empty sample n=0 is excluded rather than interpreted through the undefined1/n coefficient."
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Step 1.1 defines the map even when all sample observations are zero, and step 2.1 proves it remains measurable."
        },
