          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Proof2.1: if a unit vector attains lambda1, the nonnegative sum sum_j(lambda1-lambdaj)cj^2 vanishes, forcing every coefficient below the top eigenspace to vanish; thus the maximizer belongs to that eigenspace."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-reverse",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Proof2.1: a unit vector entirely in the leading eigenspace has Rayleigh quotient lambda1 because all occupied eigenvalues are equal to lambda1; Proof1.1 makes this quotient its projected variance, so it attains the maximum."
        }
      ],
